/* Loop Gain · the film
 *
 * The video for the script in script.md, drawn on one canvas to the
 * script's timeline and recorded silently from the browser, so that the
 * narration can be recorded over it. Every shot is either text from the
 * repository (film-data.json, generated by node from the READMEs, the
 * proofs and the bench scripts), one of the sweep figures, or the piece's
 * own models running live: the feed's line from DecayModel, the loop with
 * Bridson's growth, the plate with sand. The piece's drawing code is
 * reproduced here rather than refactored, so ../index.html stays as it is.
 *
 * One honest difference from the piece: there is no audio graph here, so
 * the loop's level is modelled from the gain (an echo sum below one, an
 * exponential to the ceiling above) rather than measured. The caption on
 * that shot says so.
 */
